# Grid B — U7 History / Authorship (feature summary, not scalar compression)
#
# Regression target: history metadata is an evidence source, not an answer
# shape. A user may ask "what feature was merged most recently" and expect a
# short feature explanation with provenance, not a collapsed `值：commitid` or
# a bare subject/hash scalar. This complements u7a/u7b, which cover scalar
# commit metadata and history counts.
#
# Ground truth drifts whenever this repository receives a new commit. Keep this
# case focused on answer shape: it must explain the latest feature/change from
# VCS history and must not collapse to a generic scalar value panel.
ID="u7c"
NAME="history — latest merged feature summary"
QUESTION="最近一次合入的是什么特性？请说明这个特性做了什么，不要只给 commit id。"
EXPECT_CONTAINS="特性"
# Do not ban the literal phrase "**值：**" here: the latest commit may itself
# be a fix about generic scalar-value rendering, and quoting that phrase is a
# valid feature explanation. Positive checks below pin the non-scalar narrative
# obligation instead.
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS=""
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="(commit|提交).*(做了什么|实质性改动|核心|功能|特性|说明|change|feature|implements)|(做了什么|实质性改动|核心|功能|特性|说明|change|feature|implements).*(commit|提交)"
